From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: set the strict duplicate filter quirk without a patch file

btbcm_finalize() sets HCI_QUIRK_STRICT_DUPLICATE_FILTER, but bcm_setup()
returns before it when no patch file was loaded. The MacBookPro15,1 has
none for its BCM4364B0 ("BCM: firmware Patch file not found"), so the
quirk is missing and a service discovery scans with "Filter duplicates:
Enabled". The controller then reports an address once per discovery
cycle of about 10.7 s. A Mac that changed its advertisement data on the
same address was reported 6 s after the change, at the next cycle.

Set the quirk on that path as well.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -597,8 +597,11 @@
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	if (!fw_load_done)
+	if (!fw_load_done) {
+		/* btbcm_finalize() sets this after loading a patch file */
+		hci_set_quirk(hu->hdev, HCI_QUIRK_STRICT_DUPLICATE_FILTER);
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	/* Init speed if any */
 	if (bcm->dev && bcm->dev->init_speed)
